    "result": "The test suite is now fully passing! Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n**Fixed Issues:**\n\n1. **Governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`):\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n\n2. **Toxicity metric signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`):\n   - Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)`\n   - This fixes how it's called from `runEvaluations` which passes `(outputs, references)` to all metrics\n   - Previously, the references array was being misinterpreted as banned terms, causing false toxicity flags\n\n**Test Results:** All 28 tests passing across 8 test files \u2713\n\nWould you like me to commit these changes?",
